1
00:00:21,856 --> 00:00:26,855
A DAIEI PRESENTATION

2
00:00:34,615 --> 00:00:36,115
"Once upon a time,

3
00:00:36,195 --> 00:00:41,956
in a forest lived a man
and his beautiful daughter.

4
00:00:43,336 --> 00:00:44,796
One day,

5
00:00:45,506 --> 00:00:49,756
a golden carriage drawn by six
horses stopped before their house.

6
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,885
Out of the carriage stepped a king.

7
00:00:53,385 --> 00:00:59,305
'Would you give me your daughter
to be my wife?' he asked the man.

8
00:01:00,345 --> 00:01:05,436
Delighted, the man agreed.

9
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:09,945
Truth be told, the king was very handsome,

10
00:01:10,606 --> 00:01:13,945
his only flaw being his
beard, which was blue.

11
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:20,455
Apart from this, there was
no fault to be found with him."

12
00:01:23,836 --> 00:01:25,666
BLUEBEARD

13
00:01:25,746 --> 00:01:29,255
-What is it?
-Nothing.

14
00:01:41,345 --> 00:01:45,476
Enough of the book.
Let's talk about something else.

15
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:47,645
Yes, please.

16
00:01:47,726 --> 00:01:49,735
-Feeling all right?
-Yes.

17
00:01:56,326 --> 00:01:57,656
I know how

18
00:01:58,656 --> 00:02:00,615
the story ends.

19
00:02:02,745 --> 00:02:07,835
In the end, the daughter kills Bluebeard.

20
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:21,326
-You are?
-Takabe, from headquarters.

21
00:03:21,405 --> 00:03:23,495
Thank you for coming.

22
00:03:23,576 --> 00:03:26,955
Mr. Takabe, do you want to see the cleaner

23
00:03:27,036 --> 00:03:29,455
-who found the body?
-No.

24
00:03:30,625 --> 00:03:34,875
A prostitute. Something like this
was bound to happen someday.

25
00:03:36,175 --> 00:03:39,546
-I'm Takabe.
-Yasukawa, from the precinct.

26
00:03:40,175 --> 00:03:42,596
-Find anything?
-Yes.

27
00:04:20,425 --> 00:04:25,976
If it was this Kuwano
guy, he took off in the raw.

28
00:04:26,636 --> 00:04:30,765
And he left us his ID.

29
00:04:34,275 --> 00:04:35,606
Excuse me.

30
00:04:43,945 --> 00:04:48,995
She was struck with a blunt object,
but she died from loss of blood.

31
00:04:49,825 --> 00:04:52,536
It wouldn't have taken long.

32
00:04:53,205 --> 00:04:57,505
Both carotid arteries
have been neatly severed.

33
00:04:58,375 --> 00:05:02,216
Have you ever seen wounds like this before?

34
00:05:02,296 --> 00:05:03,505
No.

35
00:05:04,135 --> 00:05:05,255
I see.

36
00:05:06,016 --> 00:05:09,805
But the perp is no ordinary character.

37
00:05:10,935 --> 00:05:15,516
You don't have to go this
far just to kill someone.

38
00:05:18,065 --> 00:05:22,026
The suspect may have
a motorcycle or a bicycle.

39
00:05:22,695 --> 00:05:26,695
Check all the service roads.
I'm on my way.

40
00:05:37,706 --> 00:05:40,675
I'm going to check out his neighborhood.
You want to come?

41
00:05:58,065 --> 00:06:00,315
Takabe, here.

42
00:06:06,615 --> 00:06:09,906
Then there was blood everywhere.

43
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:12,455
Lots of it.

44
00:06:12,536 --> 00:06:15,875
Sakuma, this came from
the Shibaura Precinct.

45
00:06:22,675 --> 00:06:23,925
And then

46
00:06:24,546 --> 00:06:28,925
I looked at her face —

47
00:06:31,346 --> 00:06:34,185
He looks okay to me.

48
00:06:39,476 --> 00:06:43,526
They've requested a psychiatrist.

49
00:06:43,606 --> 00:06:45,526
What's the point?

50
00:06:47,575 --> 00:06:49,406
So he's like the rest?

51
00:06:49,906 --> 00:06:54,536
Yep. Admits intent, then says
afterwards he was stunned.

52
00:06:56,455 --> 00:07:00,205
The devil made them
do it is all I can guess.

53
00:07:05,796 --> 00:07:07,505
Three cases in two months.

54
00:07:09,255 --> 00:07:10,846
What's going on?

55
00:07:11,635 --> 00:07:13,675
The media doesn't know?

56
00:07:13,766 --> 00:07:17,266
No. We haven't released any details.

57
00:07:18,305 --> 00:07:20,315
No TV or book plots like this?

58
00:07:20,856 --> 00:07:22,646
None. We checked.

59
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:25,735
No leaks, either.

60
00:07:26,856 --> 00:07:31,325
Unless you've said something
in one of your lectures.

61
00:07:31,406 --> 00:07:33,115
Give me a break!

62
00:07:33,195 --> 00:07:37,456
The perps aren't related in any
way and they're all perfectly rational.

63
00:07:38,536 --> 00:07:41,956
-So it just happened.
-"Just happened"?

64
00:07:44,125 --> 00:07:47,375
People like to think a
crime has some meaning.

65
00:07:48,046 --> 00:07:50,505
But most of them don't.

66
00:07:56,346 --> 00:07:59,266
So somebody "just happened" to do this?

67
00:09:24,266 --> 00:09:25,766
Where is this?

68
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:29,276
Shirasato Beach.

69
00:09:55,796 --> 00:09:57,136
Where is it?

70
00:09:57,636 --> 00:09:59,386
Shirasato Beach.

71
00:09:59,475 --> 00:10:00,555
Where?

72
00:10:01,055 --> 00:10:03,185
Shirasato, in Chiba.

73
00:10:03,266 --> 00:10:06,606
Shirasato? Where's that?

74
00:10:07,146 --> 00:10:08,975
Where are you going?

75
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,485
Nowhere.

76
00:11:01,036 --> 00:11:02,366
Yes?

77
00:11:02,445 --> 00:11:03,866
What's the date?

78
00:11:04,536 --> 00:11:06,126
February 26th.

79
00:11:08,876 --> 00:11:10,126
Where is this?

80
00:11:10,626 --> 00:11:12,256
I just told you.

81
00:11:12,335 --> 00:11:14,585
When was that?

82
00:11:15,085 --> 00:11:16,835
Just over there.

83
00:11:17,546 --> 00:11:21,386
Uh, do you know who I am?

84
00:11:21,886 --> 00:11:23,016
What?

85
00:11:24,095 --> 00:11:27,555
I don't know who I am.

86
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:30,396
You what?

87
00:11:34,945 --> 00:11:36,406
Help me.

88
00:11:36,906 --> 00:11:38,406
Please.

89
00:11:39,695 --> 00:11:41,406
I don't remember anything.

90
00:11:46,286 --> 00:11:49,376
-Could he use a drink?
-No, coffee's fine.

91
00:11:50,455 --> 00:11:51,626
Here.

92
00:11:56,465 --> 00:12:00,296
What's that sound out there?

93
00:12:04,266 --> 00:12:05,516
The waves.

94
00:12:12,016 --> 00:12:13,685
It's so quiet.

95
00:12:19,315 --> 00:12:24,286
"Mamiya" is written here.
Could that be your name?

96
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:27,156
I don't know.

97
00:12:27,786 --> 00:12:30,325
You could be "Mr. Mamiya."

98
00:12:31,955 --> 00:12:33,376
Mamiya?

99
00:12:35,626 --> 00:12:40,085
That's fine. Mamiya can be my name.

100
00:12:41,465 --> 00:12:43,175
It probably is.

101
00:12:44,175 --> 00:12:46,766
Maybe we should ask the police.

102
00:12:48,095 --> 00:12:50,305
No. No police.

103
00:12:50,396 --> 00:12:51,805
Why not?

104
00:13:02,065 --> 00:13:03,825
Then let's talk some more.

105
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:07,116
Perhaps your family, your work.

106
00:13:09,416 --> 00:13:11,205
First tell me about yourself.

107
00:13:13,166 --> 00:13:14,496
Me?

108
00:13:14,996 --> 00:13:19,215
I teach elementary school and I'm married.
That's it.

109
00:13:20,335 --> 00:13:21,925
Where's your wife?

110
00:13:22,425 --> 00:13:23,925
Sleeping upstairs.

111
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:26,805
Why is she doing that?

112
00:13:26,886 --> 00:13:28,266
She has a cold.

113
00:13:29,516 --> 00:13:30,555
Who does?

114
00:13:37,685 --> 00:13:38,855
Mr. Mamiya.

115
00:13:40,605 --> 00:13:41,776
Mr. Mamiya.

116
00:13:43,366 --> 00:13:44,485
Who's that?

117
00:13:45,026 --> 00:13:47,036
You, Mr. Mamiya.

118
00:13:57,046 --> 00:14:02,886
Well, I've told you about me.
Now you tell me about you.

119
00:14:04,136 --> 00:14:05,636
About me?

120
00:14:06,555 --> 00:14:07,965
Anything.

121
00:14:08,636 --> 00:14:11,345
Doesn't the name Mamiya
bring back anything?

122
00:14:13,555 --> 00:14:14,685
No.

123
00:14:16,646 --> 00:14:18,526
Why were you on the beach?

124
00:14:19,065 --> 00:14:21,855
-Where?
-Shirasato Beach.

125
00:14:25,026 --> 00:14:27,906
I don't know what you're talking about!

126
00:14:30,996 --> 00:14:33,116
Okay, let's talk about something else then.

127
00:14:33,205 --> 00:14:35,246
I want to hear about you.

128
00:14:35,916 --> 00:14:37,955
I've already told you.

129
00:14:40,876 --> 00:14:42,215
Yeah?

130
00:14:44,376 --> 00:14:46,296
I don't remember.

131
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:53,345
I teach school.
There's just me and my wife.

132
00:14:55,055 --> 00:14:56,856
What does your wife do?

133
00:14:56,935 --> 00:14:59,185
Nothing. She's a housewife.

134
00:14:59,685 --> 00:15:01,065
Who is?

135
00:15:01,146 --> 00:15:02,856
My wife.

136
00:15:07,065 --> 00:15:12,116
Oh, the woman in the pink negligee...

137
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,246
You saw her?

138
00:15:17,496 --> 00:15:22,965
I don't remember anything. You do.

139
00:15:34,305 --> 00:15:39,396
Tell me more about your wife.

140
00:15:50,825 --> 00:15:53,116
I'll be right back.

141
00:15:53,195 --> 00:15:56,246
Hello. Could you give me a minute?

142
00:16:03,705 --> 00:16:05,335
Bunch of idiots!

143
00:16:06,166 --> 00:16:07,756
What did I do wrong?

144
00:16:08,546 --> 00:16:10,296
I do things my way.

145
00:16:11,006 --> 00:16:13,555
What? Go to hell!

146
00:16:14,595 --> 00:16:18,305
Damn right I'm mad!
Stop fucking around, you dumb shit!

147
00:16:18,396 --> 00:16:19,935
Sorry to keep you.

148
00:16:20,016 --> 00:16:23,026
Here we are.

149
00:16:27,315 --> 00:16:29,656
-There you go.
-Good. Thanks.

150
00:16:29,736 --> 00:16:31,616
Thank you very much.

151
00:16:31,695 --> 00:16:34,536
Mr. Takabe, one moment.

152
00:17:35,755 --> 00:17:37,386
Hello.

153
00:17:37,465 --> 00:17:39,475
Sorry. Did I wake you?

154
00:17:40,435 --> 00:17:41,896
I'll do that.

155
00:17:41,975 --> 00:17:43,356
No, I will...

156
00:17:43,435 --> 00:17:45,856
No, I feel good today.

157
00:17:56,195 --> 00:17:57,945
Where's the opener?

158
00:18:00,116 --> 00:18:01,285
Here.

159
00:18:13,965 --> 00:18:17,755
-I poured you some beer.
-Thanks.

160
00:18:27,146 --> 00:18:29,435
How's work? Busy?

161
00:18:30,185 --> 00:18:33,566
Yeah. How about you?

162
00:18:33,656 --> 00:18:38,445
Me? I just did nothing all day long.

163
00:18:54,086 --> 00:18:55,255
Fumie.

164
00:18:58,425 --> 00:19:02,015
When this case is over,
let's take a trip somewhere.

165
00:19:03,636 --> 00:19:05,396
Oh, that's all right...

166
00:19:05,475 --> 00:19:08,646
No, I'd like to go somewhere.

167
00:19:10,685 --> 00:19:15,156
We're definitely going. You decide where.

168
00:19:15,816 --> 00:19:17,275
Where?

169
00:19:17,366 --> 00:19:22,076
I'll leave that up to you.
Okinawa, Hokkaido, anywhere.

170
00:19:24,116 --> 00:19:26,535
From one extreme to the other.

171
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,495
You decide.

172
00:19:32,705 --> 00:19:34,086
All right.

173
00:20:21,596 --> 00:20:23,386
The victim is

174
00:20:23,465 --> 00:20:28,056
Tomoko Hanaoka, 26, the suspect's wife.

175
00:20:28,136 --> 00:20:30,806
Her carotid arteries were cut.

176
00:20:32,725 --> 00:20:38,695
"Suspect teaches elementary school.
Committed to his work, a good teacher.

177
00:20:39,525 --> 00:20:44,366
High school classmates, married two years.

178
00:20:44,445 --> 00:20:46,785
Neighbors describe them as a fine couple.

179
00:20:47,906 --> 00:20:50,416
No trouble with debt or anything."

180
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:53,416
The devil made him do it?

181
00:21:18,066 --> 00:21:19,275
Mr. Hanaoka,

182
00:21:19,985 --> 00:21:23,695
last night you killed your wife Tomoko.

183
00:21:24,735 --> 00:21:26,445
Is that correct?

184
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:29,745
Mr. Hanaoka?

185
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:35,666
You sliced her open with a knife

186
00:21:36,586 --> 00:21:40,675
from throat to chest.

187
00:21:43,215 --> 00:21:44,596
Why?

188
00:21:46,505 --> 00:21:48,675
Why did you kill her like that?

189
00:21:50,015 --> 00:21:53,515
I don't know. Why did I do it?

190
00:21:55,435 --> 00:21:58,935
Did you read some novel
or see some movie like that?

191
00:22:01,525 --> 00:22:03,316
Did someone talk to you?

192
00:22:04,866 --> 00:22:06,025
No.

193
00:22:08,866 --> 00:22:10,285
I see.

194
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:16,376
Did you hate your wife?

195
00:22:19,545 --> 00:22:24,675
Things weren't going well
between you, were they?

196
00:22:25,386 --> 00:22:27,636
No, that's not true.

197
00:22:28,175 --> 00:22:29,715
Then isn't it strange?

198
00:22:31,886 --> 00:22:34,146
What is it, Mr. Hanaoka?

199
00:22:45,066 --> 00:22:47,406
I remember everything.

200
00:22:48,576 --> 00:22:52,535
I killed Tomoko.
At the time it just seemed

201
00:22:54,035 --> 00:22:56,576
the natural thing to do.

202
00:22:59,745 --> 00:23:02,755
-Was there a quarrel?
-No.

203
00:23:03,425 --> 00:23:06,715
It's weird.
You murdered your wife for no reason?

204
00:23:09,596 --> 00:23:13,556
That's right. There was no reason.

205
00:23:15,896 --> 00:23:20,896
But I killed her! I killed Tomoko!

206
00:23:25,156 --> 00:23:27,985
Mr. Hanaoka, crying won't help.

207
00:23:28,945 --> 00:23:32,745
I'm going to keep on
asking you until you tell me.

208
00:23:33,745 --> 00:23:36,705
-I'm sure this is hard for you —
-That's enough, Takabe.

209
00:23:36,785 --> 00:23:38,995
-No.
-That's enough.

210
00:23:40,455 --> 00:23:41,705
Take him.

211
00:23:44,255 --> 00:23:47,636
He's not lying. He remembers everything.

212
00:23:48,175 --> 00:23:51,056
Chances are he's completely sane.

213
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:01,225
Hey! Stop that!

214
00:24:02,185 --> 00:24:07,816
Would a person cut someone up like
that because the devil made them do it?

215
00:24:15,826 --> 00:24:21,705
What if they all had some
similar trauma in their childhoods?

216
00:24:22,455 --> 00:24:27,255
It lies suppressed for
years, then they explode.

217
00:24:27,336 --> 00:24:28,755
Could that happen?

218
00:24:29,255 --> 00:24:32,346
Since when did you become a shrink?

219
00:24:33,096 --> 00:24:37,725
I've been reading up. You know, my wife...

220
00:24:38,475 --> 00:24:40,975
Don't laugh. Beginners' books.

221
00:24:42,475 --> 00:24:46,025
Don't believe everything you read.

222
00:24:46,525 --> 00:24:48,316
Well, it's in a book.

223
00:24:49,356 --> 00:24:53,366
No one can understand
what motivates a criminal,

224
00:24:53,445 --> 00:24:55,616
sometimes not even the criminal.

225
00:24:55,695 --> 00:24:59,035
No one understands.

226
00:25:03,455 --> 00:25:05,916
You're getting in too deep.

227
00:25:06,545 --> 00:25:12,175
No. All I want is to find words
that will explain the crimes.

228
00:25:14,675 --> 00:25:16,386
That's my job.

229
00:25:17,886 --> 00:25:19,806
Yeah, I guess so.

230
00:25:22,556 --> 00:25:25,606
How is your wife, by the way?

231
00:25:26,725 --> 00:25:30,156
She's going to the
hospital you recommended.

232
00:25:31,906 --> 00:25:34,116
She's a lot better.

233
00:25:34,906 --> 00:25:36,235
Yeah?

234
00:25:38,616 --> 00:25:40,576
At least, it seems that way.

235
00:25:41,995 --> 00:25:43,586
I don't know if she really is.

236
00:25:45,795 --> 00:25:48,416
-Thank you very much.
-That's all right.

237
00:25:48,505 --> 00:25:51,005
-I might have to come again.
-You might?

238
00:25:51,086 --> 00:25:54,295
Could you contact this officer
if someone else moves in?

239
00:25:54,386 --> 00:25:56,755
-All right.
-Give him your number.

240
00:26:57,485 --> 00:27:01,616
Hey, you! What are you doing up there?

241
00:27:03,156 --> 00:27:06,535
You'll get hurt! Come down!

242
00:27:17,045 --> 00:27:19,346
I'm coming up!

243
00:27:23,596 --> 00:27:24,975
Damn fool!

244
00:27:26,265 --> 00:27:29,185
Name, address and particulars unknown.

245
00:27:29,685 --> 00:27:34,025
He appears to be in his late 20s.

246
00:27:35,406 --> 00:27:37,985
Yes, I know that.

247
00:27:39,025 --> 00:27:41,535
All right, thank you.

248
00:27:45,826 --> 00:27:48,535
Well, the station is looking
for information on you,

249
00:27:49,035 --> 00:27:51,295
but if you yourself don't know...

250
00:27:51,376 --> 00:27:53,126
The computer has nothing either.

251
00:28:04,725 --> 00:28:08,185
Don't worry.
Tomorrow we'll get you to a hospital.

252
00:28:08,685 --> 00:28:10,646
Have some tea.

253
00:28:14,485 --> 00:28:16,356
Is this your place?

254
00:28:17,856 --> 00:28:20,066
No, it's a police box.

255
00:28:22,076 --> 00:28:24,616
-You're a cop?
-Yes.

256
00:28:30,745 --> 00:28:33,126
Why am I talking to you?

257
00:28:34,755 --> 00:28:37,755
I want to ask you some questions.

258
00:28:40,596 --> 00:28:42,056
About me?

259
00:28:44,136 --> 00:28:48,806
Do you remember standing on that roof?

260
00:28:52,265 --> 00:28:55,775
What about coming to
this police box with me?

261
00:28:59,775 --> 00:29:01,616
Is this a police box?

262
00:29:03,275 --> 00:29:04,535
Yes.

263
00:29:09,666 --> 00:29:11,245
Who are you?

264
00:29:15,876 --> 00:29:17,505
Oh, boy!

265
00:29:18,465 --> 00:29:20,126
Okay, enough.

266
00:29:23,465 --> 00:29:25,765
-May I smoke?
-Sure.

267
00:29:27,306 --> 00:29:30,646
-You can't smoke here.
-That's okay.

268
00:29:39,646 --> 00:29:40,775
Here.

269
00:29:42,025 --> 00:29:43,525
I'm on duty.

270
00:29:44,616 --> 00:29:45,735
Oh.

271
00:29:51,826 --> 00:29:54,245
-Here.
-Oh, thanks.

272
00:29:56,836 --> 00:29:58,626
I'll go do my rounds.

273
00:30:15,515 --> 00:30:17,475
It must be hard work.

274
00:30:17,975 --> 00:30:20,695
Sometimes.

275
00:30:40,545 --> 00:30:41,836
I'm sleepy.

276
00:30:44,636 --> 00:30:46,215
I'm gonna sleep a bit.

277
00:30:47,045 --> 00:30:48,215
Okay.

278
00:31:20,666 --> 00:31:21,916
Mr. Oida.

279
00:31:26,255 --> 00:31:27,795
Look at this.

280
00:31:39,975 --> 00:31:41,896
You hear me, don't you?

281
00:31:42,985 --> 00:31:44,106
Yes.

282
00:31:45,606 --> 00:31:47,156
You know what I'd like?

283
00:31:48,525 --> 00:31:50,485
I'd like to hear about you.

284
00:31:51,406 --> 00:31:52,616
Huh?

285
00:31:55,785 --> 00:31:57,285
Tell me.

286
00:32:07,636 --> 00:32:10,215
I think it's the flu.

287
00:32:14,636 --> 00:32:16,685
Does your throat hurt?

288
00:32:16,765 --> 00:32:18,475
A little.

289
00:32:21,765 --> 00:32:24,396
Lower your trousers and lie down, please.

290
00:32:24,485 --> 00:32:25,646
What?

291
00:32:30,485 --> 00:32:32,695
Lower your trousers and lie down.

292
00:32:33,826 --> 00:32:34,906
Okay.

293
00:32:54,556 --> 00:32:56,306
That's good enough.

294
00:33:00,185 --> 00:33:02,185
Raise your knees a bit.

295
00:33:08,356 --> 00:33:10,195
You're not shy, are you!

296
00:33:11,406 --> 00:33:13,326
Your lymph glands are a bit swollen.

297
00:33:13,826 --> 00:33:15,406
Fine, thank you.

298
00:33:40,056 --> 00:33:42,306
What do you want at this hour?

299
00:33:42,396 --> 00:33:44,566
Sorry. This won't take long.

300
00:33:46,435 --> 00:33:49,485
Ten minutes, and that's all.

301
00:33:50,525 --> 00:33:51,945
Listen,

302
00:33:52,656 --> 00:33:56,076
you don't think it might be
some kind of hypnosis, do you?

303
00:33:56,156 --> 00:33:57,495
Huh?

304
00:33:57,576 --> 00:34:00,916
You know, someone
looks at a flashing light,

305
00:34:00,995 --> 00:34:03,826
then does whatever someone else tells them?

306
00:34:03,916 --> 00:34:06,205
"Hypnotic suggestion."

307
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:10,795
Is it possible? What do you think?

308
00:34:12,215 --> 00:34:14,465
You're the only one I dare ask.

309
00:34:15,675 --> 00:34:18,596
-Well?
-Got some new evidence?

310
00:34:19,136 --> 00:34:20,846
Just an idea.

311
00:34:23,015 --> 00:34:27,106
Hypnotism itself is a
very common technique.

312
00:34:27,725 --> 00:34:31,025
But even if you manage
to hypnotize someone,

313
00:34:31,105 --> 00:34:34,445
you can't change their basic moral sense.

314
00:34:34,945 --> 00:34:39,036
A person who thinks
murder is evil won't kill anyone

315
00:34:39,116 --> 00:34:41,286
under hypnotic suggestion.

316
00:34:48,415 --> 00:34:54,295
Could you induce someone
to cut in that "X" pattern?

317
00:34:56,346 --> 00:35:00,726
It would take forever to get a
suggestion like that into place.

318
00:35:00,806 --> 00:35:03,766
-It's impossible?
-I didn't say that.

319
00:35:04,266 --> 00:35:07,145
If the hypnotist was a genius...

320
00:35:08,315 --> 00:35:10,645
But why would someone do that?

321
00:35:12,315 --> 00:35:13,445
I don't know.

322
00:35:13,525 --> 00:35:18,616
A thrill killing? Some thrill that'd be.

323
00:35:20,195 --> 00:35:24,826
You said yourself that no one
knows what motivates a criminal.

324
00:36:14,255 --> 00:36:18,215
Mr. Oida, do you know where
the stuff for the Ward Office is?

325
00:36:18,295 --> 00:36:20,136
The right-hand shelf.

326
00:36:22,556 --> 00:36:25,726
-Yeah, here it is.
-Like I said.

327
00:36:34,895 --> 00:36:36,395
Be right back.

328
00:37:29,616 --> 00:37:30,616
Come in.

329
00:37:33,165 --> 00:37:35,125
Sorry I'm late.

330
00:37:35,206 --> 00:37:38,545
That's all right. Did something happen?

331
00:37:38,625 --> 00:37:41,425
-I got lost.
-Lost?

332
00:37:42,005 --> 00:37:43,255
Yes.

333
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:45,886
Did you come another way?

334
00:37:46,425 --> 00:37:51,846
I don't know.
Suddenly I just didn't know where I was.

335
00:37:52,976 --> 00:37:55,105
How did you get here, then?

336
00:37:56,065 --> 00:37:57,605
I don't know.

337
00:37:59,025 --> 00:38:02,355
Suddenly I was in front of the hospital.

338
00:38:04,065 --> 00:38:07,786
Well, it all worked out for the best.
You got here.

339
00:38:07,866 --> 00:38:09,036
Yes.

340
00:38:09,786 --> 00:38:10,915
That book...

341
00:38:12,956 --> 00:38:16,165
It's Bluebeard. Do you remember it?

342
00:38:20,005 --> 00:38:22,465
No, I've never seen it before.

343
00:38:30,766 --> 00:38:33,096
There's nothing physically wrong.

344
00:38:34,645 --> 00:38:38,065
Just a sprained ankle.
Nothing to worry about.

345
00:38:40,186 --> 00:38:43,695
So how's your memory?

346
00:38:48,195 --> 00:38:54,206
Tomorrow we'll move you to a hospital
with a proper psychiatric department.

347
00:38:55,326 --> 00:38:56,415
Sure.

348
00:39:04,715 --> 00:39:10,556
How far back do you remember?

349
00:39:13,726 --> 00:39:17,306
I remember talking to you.

350
00:39:17,395 --> 00:39:18,476
Any worries?

351
00:39:18,565 --> 00:39:21,235
Worries? About what?

352
00:39:22,395 --> 00:39:24,145
You're quite calm.

353
00:39:28,866 --> 00:39:30,945
You're the one with worries.

354
00:39:31,866 --> 00:39:32,996
Sorry?

355
00:39:34,665 --> 00:39:36,165
May I smoke?

356
00:39:36,665 --> 00:39:38,456
There's no smoking here.

357
00:39:38,956 --> 00:39:40,206
I see.

358
00:39:47,425 --> 00:39:50,096
What do you mean, I have worries?

359
00:39:52,886 --> 00:39:54,726
Uh, what?

360
00:39:56,395 --> 00:39:57,726
I forget.

361
00:40:03,775 --> 00:40:05,025
Water.

362
00:40:42,016 --> 00:40:46,105
Doctor, can I tell you something?

363
00:40:47,906 --> 00:40:49,156
Certainly.

364
00:40:50,156 --> 00:40:54,695
All the things that used to be inside me,

365
00:40:55,576 --> 00:40:57,326
now they're all outside.

366
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:00,496
So,

367
00:41:01,415 --> 00:41:06,795
I can see all of the
things inside you, Doctor.

368
00:41:09,965 --> 00:41:12,136
But the inside of me

369
00:41:13,925 --> 00:41:15,636
is empty.

370
00:41:49,335 --> 00:41:50,795
Don't look at me.

371
00:41:57,386 --> 00:41:59,766
Now you tell me about yourself.

372
00:42:01,306 --> 00:42:04,226
About me? What about me?

373
00:42:05,976 --> 00:42:07,645
Why you became a doctor.

374
00:42:08,775 --> 00:42:10,105
Why?

375
00:42:11,025 --> 00:42:14,315
You're just a woman.
Why did you become a doctor?

376
00:42:15,616 --> 00:42:17,195
Just a woman?

377
00:42:21,366 --> 00:42:25,915
That's what people said, isn't it?

378
00:42:28,255 --> 00:42:29,755
They did, didn't they?

379
00:42:31,505 --> 00:42:33,045
Think back.

380
00:42:34,425 --> 00:42:37,505
Remember exactly how you felt.

381
00:42:40,675 --> 00:42:42,346
Just a woman.

382
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:51,445
Woman is a lower life form than man.
Isn't she?

383
00:42:57,735 --> 00:43:01,996
See? Now you remember.

384
00:43:04,165 --> 00:43:06,076
When you were in medical school,

385
00:43:07,915 --> 00:43:11,835
you dissected a corpse, didn't you?

386
00:43:14,295 --> 00:43:16,045
The first corpse you'd ever seen.

387
00:43:17,505 --> 00:43:19,136
It was a man, wasn't it?

388
00:43:21,306 --> 00:43:22,806
Think back.

389
00:43:24,556 --> 00:43:26,855
You'd never seen a naked man before.

390
00:43:28,565 --> 00:43:32,355
You took your scalpel and cut into him.

391
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:38,866
It made you feel good, didn't it?

392
00:43:40,485 --> 00:43:41,746
Didn't it?

393
00:43:42,956 --> 00:43:44,076
Think back.

394
00:43:45,576 --> 00:43:47,996
You wanted to be a surgeon,

395
00:43:49,085 --> 00:43:53,625
but you weren't sure you
could, and you ended up a GP.

396
00:43:55,335 --> 00:43:56,505
No.

397
00:43:58,175 --> 00:44:03,136
What you really wanted
to do was cut a man open.

398
00:45:07,576 --> 00:45:09,665
You shot him in the head.

399
00:45:10,456 --> 00:45:12,415
Wasn't that enough?

400
00:45:15,415 --> 00:45:21,636
Is there a reason why you cut
into the dead man with a knife?

401
00:45:22,795 --> 00:45:23,925
Yes.

402
00:45:25,175 --> 00:45:28,476
He was someone I didn't like.

403
00:45:28,556 --> 00:45:29,806
Why?

404
00:45:31,145 --> 00:45:32,645
Many reasons.

405
00:45:34,436 --> 00:45:38,985
It's been three years since
he was transferred to our box.

406
00:45:40,105 --> 00:45:42,025
I put up with him all the time.

407
00:45:43,695 --> 00:45:48,036
Finally I couldn't stand it anymore.

408
00:45:48,116 --> 00:45:49,616
But to kill him?

409
00:45:50,706 --> 00:45:51,826
Yes.

410
00:45:52,746 --> 00:45:57,045
Detective, you've never
killed anyone, have you?

411
00:45:59,375 --> 00:46:03,505
That's how you get when you hate
someone from the bottom of your heart.

412
00:46:04,096 --> 00:46:06,846
So it was an angry impulse?

413
00:46:07,556 --> 00:46:10,596
No. I was completely calm.

414
00:46:13,936 --> 00:46:17,105
Isn't that a bit strange?

415
00:46:18,855 --> 00:46:21,906
Yes, it definitely is strange.

416
00:46:22,906 --> 00:46:24,195
May I?

417
00:46:27,036 --> 00:46:29,326
I'm Sakuma, a psychiatrist.

418
00:46:30,076 --> 00:46:34,915
Officer Oida, do you remember
seeing anything shiny?

419
00:46:34,996 --> 00:46:36,335
For example,

420
00:46:37,835 --> 00:46:39,375
something like this?

421
00:46:41,835 --> 00:46:42,875
No.

422
00:46:44,136 --> 00:46:47,846
Were you talking to
anyone before the crime?

423
00:46:48,766 --> 00:46:49,886
No.

424
00:46:52,136 --> 00:46:55,806
Is that true? Try to remember.

425
00:46:56,355 --> 00:47:00,105
Do you think you could
stop doing that, please?

426
00:47:00,186 --> 00:47:01,485
Keep going.

427
00:47:02,025 --> 00:47:03,565
Don't stop!

428
00:47:04,275 --> 00:47:08,025
You did talk to someone, didn't you?

429
00:47:08,116 --> 00:47:11,076
We know you did. Look at the light.

430
00:47:12,366 --> 00:47:13,706
No. No one.

431
00:47:13,786 --> 00:47:16,326
Yes, you did. Who was it?

432
00:47:16,415 --> 00:47:18,125
What was his name?

433
00:47:18,206 --> 00:47:19,335
I didn't!

434
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:23,175
-Enough.
-Mr. Oida.

435
00:47:25,585 --> 00:47:29,505
You must have seen a light like this.

436
00:47:29,596 --> 00:47:31,215
Was anyone there?

437
00:47:32,596 --> 00:47:35,936
Someone told you to do this, didn't they?

438
00:47:37,226 --> 00:47:38,726
Who was it?

439
00:47:39,686 --> 00:47:45,485
There might have been someone there.

440
00:47:45,565 --> 00:47:47,565
-Was there?
-I don't know!

441
00:47:47,656 --> 00:47:51,286
Of course you know. Who was it?

442
00:47:51,906 --> 00:47:53,706
Tell me his name, please.

443
00:47:55,246 --> 00:47:59,956
-His name?
-Yes, his name. What was his name?

444
00:48:01,835 --> 00:48:04,835
He... didn't have a name.

445
00:48:04,925 --> 00:48:09,005
What do you mean?
Mr. Oida, look at the light.

446
00:48:09,096 --> 00:48:10,636
That's enough.

447
00:48:26,605 --> 00:48:29,775
Excuse me. I'm thirsty.

448
00:48:40,536 --> 00:48:42,375
It is hypnosis.

449
00:48:42,456 --> 00:48:45,045
We can't be sure of that.

450
00:48:45,125 --> 00:48:47,375
But that wasn't normal.

451
00:48:47,465 --> 00:48:49,755
I decide what's normal.

452
00:48:50,795 --> 00:48:52,675
Stop traumatizing people.

453
00:48:52,755 --> 00:48:58,056
Sakuma, we're not counseling
this man, we're interrogating him.

454
00:49:13,985 --> 00:49:15,406
-Don't move!
-But...

455
00:49:15,496 --> 00:49:16,906
Just stay there.

456
00:49:58,616 --> 00:50:00,866
Mr. Oida? Mr. Oida?

457
00:50:03,335 --> 00:50:05,665
What was that you just did?

458
00:50:06,835 --> 00:50:09,165
Just now? Nothing.

459
00:50:09,665 --> 00:50:12,045
What's that motion you're
making with your hand?

460
00:50:14,505 --> 00:50:15,755
This?

461
00:50:20,976 --> 00:50:22,145
I don't know.

462
00:50:23,976 --> 00:50:25,976
Nothing in particular.

463
00:50:26,476 --> 00:50:28,985
Tell me about what you just did.

464
00:50:35,866 --> 00:50:38,996
I was just thinking of Officer Tamura.

465
00:50:41,866 --> 00:50:43,375
That's all.

466
00:50:44,665 --> 00:50:48,375
Nothing more than that.

467
00:51:38,136 --> 00:51:40,596
How long will this go on?

468
00:51:42,175 --> 00:51:43,346
Here we go.

469
00:51:50,605 --> 00:51:51,775
Mr. Takabe!

470
00:51:54,855 --> 00:51:56,565
What are you doing?

471
00:51:56,656 --> 00:52:00,076
Another murder. The restrooms
in Chuo Park. Get over there.

472
00:52:00,156 --> 00:52:05,786
There was a report of a suspicious
person at Shiomicho Hospital.

473
00:52:06,366 --> 00:52:08,496
Oida took him in there.

474
00:52:21,505 --> 00:52:23,386
-Amnesia?
-Apparently.

475
00:52:23,476 --> 00:52:26,266
-Where is he?
-He's not in his room.

476
00:52:26,936 --> 00:52:29,605
-So where is he?
-They say he hasn't left.

477
00:53:28,956 --> 00:53:30,956
I know you're here.

478
00:53:41,175 --> 00:53:43,675
Step out here, please.

479
00:53:44,925 --> 00:53:47,846
-Where?
-Here.

480
00:53:48,636 --> 00:53:51,976
I don't know where "here" is.

481
00:53:52,056 --> 00:53:55,686
Well, then, I'll have to come to you.

482
00:54:08,906 --> 00:54:10,076
Where are you?

483
00:54:12,286 --> 00:54:13,536
Come out.

484
00:54:15,206 --> 00:54:16,746
Who are you?

485
00:54:20,925 --> 00:54:22,425
Police.

486
00:54:22,925 --> 00:54:24,096
Who?

487
00:54:25,045 --> 00:54:26,596
A police officer.

488
00:54:29,266 --> 00:54:31,556
Do you understand my question?

489
00:54:33,686 --> 00:54:36,645
I've got some questions to ask you.

490
00:54:41,105 --> 00:54:43,406
I want to hear about you.

491
00:54:43,485 --> 00:54:46,366
I ask the questions! You answer!

492
00:54:48,156 --> 00:54:49,656
Who are you?

493
00:54:50,786 --> 00:54:51,956
Where are you?

494
00:54:53,326 --> 00:54:56,246
-Who are you?
-A detective!

495
00:54:58,045 --> 00:54:59,875
Stop screwing around!

496
00:55:10,806 --> 00:55:12,306
Name?

497
00:55:14,846 --> 00:55:16,355
I forget.

498
00:55:19,186 --> 00:55:21,355
Address? Age? Occupation?

499
00:55:23,565 --> 00:55:24,906
Don't know.

500
00:55:28,735 --> 00:55:30,906
When were you checked in?

501
00:55:33,206 --> 00:55:34,665
Where?

502
00:55:34,746 --> 00:55:36,536
The hospital.

503
00:55:37,536 --> 00:55:39,085
Shiomicho Hospital.

504
00:55:39,706 --> 00:55:43,255
You saw Dr. Miyajima.

505
00:55:46,465 --> 00:55:47,596
Where?

506
00:55:50,766 --> 00:55:52,306
We're going in circles.

507
00:56:14,706 --> 00:56:17,665
Have you ever met any of these people?

508
00:56:20,625 --> 00:56:21,956
I don't remember.

509
00:56:28,505 --> 00:56:31,425
How about this person?

510
00:56:36,976 --> 00:56:38,145
I don't know.

511
00:56:39,476 --> 00:56:41,726
This is you.

512
00:56:59,706 --> 00:57:00,915
It looks like me.

513
00:57:01,415 --> 00:57:04,005
So now we're sure of one thing.

514
00:57:04,505 --> 00:57:06,715
That's you. All right?

515
00:57:08,175 --> 00:57:10,005
I don't know him.

516
00:57:11,925 --> 00:57:13,425
So this is me?

517
00:57:19,806 --> 00:57:21,056
Who are you?

518
00:57:23,186 --> 00:57:25,815
A detective. How about these?

519
00:57:32,076 --> 00:57:33,275
Corpses.

520
00:57:35,695 --> 00:57:37,956
-Do you like these?
-No.

521
00:57:39,826 --> 00:57:43,415
If you don't like them,
why do you have them?

522
00:57:43,996 --> 00:57:45,375
It's my job.

523
00:57:46,835 --> 00:57:47,965
Job?

524
00:57:50,295 --> 00:57:51,835
What's your job?

525
00:57:53,505 --> 00:57:56,215
Right now, asking you questions.

526
00:57:58,096 --> 00:57:59,226
Why?

527
00:58:00,016 --> 00:58:03,306
You're an important source of information.

528
00:58:04,645 --> 00:58:07,565
Me? Why?

529
00:58:11,195 --> 00:58:15,116
We found your fingerprints
at the Hanaoka house.

530
00:58:15,195 --> 00:58:20,786
Whether you remember or not, you know him.

531
00:58:23,746 --> 00:58:27,165
Oh, is that what you mean?

532
00:58:30,125 --> 00:58:32,085
You know a lot, Detective.

533
00:58:33,045 --> 00:58:35,636
Not what's inside your head.

534
00:58:37,465 --> 00:58:38,636
My head?

535
00:58:45,936 --> 00:58:47,105
Here?

536
00:58:50,945 --> 00:58:54,906
Your attitude isn't helping you at all.

537
00:58:55,735 --> 00:58:56,906
Why?

538
00:58:58,945 --> 00:59:01,786
Right. I want you to try and
remember from the beginning.

539
00:59:02,826 --> 00:59:08,125
You admit you were in Shiomicho Hospital?

540
00:59:08,746 --> 00:59:12,045
What's wrong?
Why are you raising your voice?

541
00:59:13,085 --> 00:59:14,715
Because you won't answer.

542
00:59:14,795 --> 00:59:17,806
-Why?
-Answer my questions.

543
00:59:17,886 --> 00:59:19,306
May I smoke?

544
00:59:22,766 --> 00:59:24,436
-No.
-Takabe.

545
00:59:30,605 --> 00:59:31,775
Detective?

546
00:59:33,195 --> 00:59:34,315
Yes?

547
00:59:36,275 --> 00:59:39,616
Tell me more about yourself.

548
00:59:41,906 --> 00:59:43,536
After you talk.

549
00:59:44,036 --> 00:59:46,576
Stop it! Leave him alone!

550
00:59:55,585 --> 00:59:58,346
I need to examine him,

551
00:59:58,425 --> 01:00:01,846
but I see clear symptoms
of typical psychosis.

552
01:00:03,306 --> 01:00:04,806
Don't get into it with him.

553
01:00:06,895 --> 01:00:08,355
You'll just get angry.

554
01:00:18,565 --> 01:00:21,036
Hey, you all right?

555
01:00:21,826 --> 01:00:23,496
Yeah. I'm all right.

556
01:01:41,945 --> 01:01:46,246
I went out to the convenience
store, and I got lost.

557
01:01:47,906 --> 01:01:49,036
I see.

558
01:01:50,536 --> 01:01:52,625
We'll need toothbrushes.

559
01:01:53,456 --> 01:01:55,706
We will, won't we?

560
01:01:57,085 --> 01:02:01,085
What if we stay at a hotel

561
01:02:01,175 --> 01:02:04,715
where they don't give you one?

562
01:02:11,645 --> 01:02:16,025
I'll do the shopping, okay?

563
01:02:19,645 --> 01:02:22,815
You're tired.

564
01:02:24,275 --> 01:02:26,326
You don't have to do everything for me.

565
01:02:30,116 --> 01:02:33,915
We don't have to take a trip, either.

566
01:02:38,255 --> 01:02:42,045
We'll take that trip. Definitely.

567
01:02:44,465 --> 01:02:46,215
My next holiday.

568
01:02:53,346 --> 01:02:54,436
For sure.

569
01:02:56,186 --> 01:02:57,315
Hey.

570
01:02:57,815 --> 01:03:00,025
Impound all that guy's stuff.

571
01:03:00,105 --> 01:03:04,116
But he's a witness, not a suspect.

572
01:03:04,195 --> 01:03:06,116
I don't care. The works.

573
01:03:21,625 --> 01:03:23,085
What's that?

574
01:03:23,175 --> 01:03:26,505
A scar from a burn. Not very old.

575
01:03:27,005 --> 01:03:30,016
Possibly caused by contact with metal.

576
01:03:30,886 --> 01:03:32,976
Something round and hot.

577
01:03:33,556 --> 01:03:35,056
Round and hot.

578
01:04:07,545 --> 01:04:08,846
This way.

579
01:04:25,105 --> 01:04:26,945
No one's home.

580
01:04:27,025 --> 01:04:29,065
-Do you have the key?
-Yeah.

581
01:04:32,616 --> 01:04:35,406
Is Mr. Mamiya in some kind of trouble?

582
01:04:35,915 --> 01:04:37,746
That's what I'm here to find out.

583
01:04:37,826 --> 01:04:40,335
I see. Well, it's all yours.

584
01:04:42,585 --> 01:04:43,755
Excuse me.

585
01:04:44,915 --> 01:04:47,425
When did you last see Mr. Mamiya?

586
01:04:48,085 --> 01:04:51,425
About six months ago, maybe.

587
01:04:51,925 --> 01:04:54,096
I don't come out here much.

588
01:04:54,596 --> 01:04:56,936
He paid a year's rent in advance.

589
01:04:57,686 --> 01:04:59,686
I'll be downstairs if you need me.

590
01:05:24,915 --> 01:05:28,625
SEVERE PERSONALITY DISORDERS:
PSYCHOTHERAPEUTIC STRATEGIES

591
01:05:30,675 --> 01:05:33,965
PSYCHODYNAMIC PSYCHOTHERAPY
OF BORDERLINE PATIENTS

592
01:05:35,806 --> 01:05:38,516
THE THEORY OF PSYCHOANALYSIS
BY CARL GUSTAV JUNG

593
01:05:47,775 --> 01:05:50,355
PERSONALITY DISORDER

594
01:05:53,406 --> 01:05:54,906
MESMERISM AND THE END

595
01:05:54,907 --> 01:05:56,406
OF THE ENLIGHTENMENT IN FRANCE

596
01:05:57,326 --> 01:06:00,326
MESMER, OU L'EXTASE MAGNÉTIQUE

597
01:06:16,175 --> 01:06:19,266
ANIMAL MAGNETISM
AND ITS PSYCHOLOGICAL EFFECTS

598
01:06:22,855 --> 01:06:24,540
KUNIHIKO MAMIYA

599
01:06:24,541 --> 01:06:26,226
MUSASHINO MEDICAL UNIVERSITY

600
01:06:41,415 --> 01:06:43,286
MAY CAUSE A "SPASM"...

601
01:06:43,375 --> 01:06:45,206
FALLS INTO A COMA...

602
01:06:45,286 --> 01:06:47,875
MESMERISM

603
01:07:36,636 --> 01:07:40,056
Sakuma, I've found out who our man is.

604
01:07:41,226 --> 01:07:43,266
Kunihiko Mamiya.

605
01:07:43,346 --> 01:07:46,806
A psychology student
up until three years ago.

606
01:07:47,936 --> 01:07:52,025
His professors said he
hardly showed up for classes.

607
01:07:53,025 --> 01:07:54,945
Yeah, just like you.

608
01:07:55,525 --> 01:08:00,116
Then he was a live-in part-timer
at a junkyard in Kawasaki.

609
01:08:01,445 --> 01:08:03,906
That's probably where he got burned.

610
01:08:04,786 --> 01:08:06,496
Vanished six months ago.

611
01:08:07,915 --> 01:08:10,915
No, I don't know what he was doing.

612
01:08:13,125 --> 01:08:16,795
Have you ever heard of Mesmer?

613
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:26,096
Okay. Tell me when I get back.

614
01:09:39,716 --> 01:09:43,426
What's wrong? What happened?

615
01:09:48,515 --> 01:09:51,765
Don't scare me like that. Are you ill?

616
01:09:53,565 --> 01:09:55,225
Why are you home now?

617
01:09:57,435 --> 01:09:59,145
It's nothing.

618
01:09:59,815 --> 01:10:02,826
He's ill. I've moved him to the hospital.

619
01:10:02,906 --> 01:10:05,656
-On whose authority?
-My own.

620
01:10:06,246 --> 01:10:09,036
-Are you trying to take him away from me?
-That's right.

621
01:10:09,116 --> 01:10:12,456
It's dangerous to let you
keep talking to that man.

622
01:10:13,916 --> 01:10:15,496
You bastard.

623
01:10:16,626 --> 01:10:20,466
-Hey! What about Mesmer?
-I'll ask him.

624
01:10:30,385 --> 01:10:32,095
No one's supposed to see him.

625
01:10:33,975 --> 01:10:35,145
Open up.

626
01:10:46,286 --> 01:10:47,445
Move.

627
01:11:06,805 --> 01:11:10,095
What's wrong? Your hands are shaking.

628
01:11:17,645 --> 01:11:18,975
I found out.

629
01:11:20,895 --> 01:11:25,445
Your name is Kunihiko Mamiya.

630
01:11:27,275 --> 01:11:28,576
Is that right?

631
01:11:28,656 --> 01:11:32,956
Mamiya, who is this man called Mesmer?

632
01:11:33,916 --> 01:11:35,076
Who?

633
01:11:35,706 --> 01:11:37,086
Mesmer.

634
01:11:38,836 --> 01:11:42,376
At the university you studied about Mesmer

635
01:11:42,876 --> 01:11:45,086
and hypnotic suggestion.

636
01:11:46,176 --> 01:11:47,345
What?

637
01:11:48,676 --> 01:11:50,765
Whether you remember or not,

638
01:11:51,595 --> 01:11:57,265
I'm going to have you arraigned
on charges of incitement to murder.

639
01:11:59,355 --> 01:12:01,145
It's over.

640
01:12:07,195 --> 01:12:09,866
You saw your wife dead, didn't you?

641
01:12:17,706 --> 01:12:20,376
Your wife is ill, isn't she?

642
01:12:23,126 --> 01:12:25,506
Is it hard caring for her at home?

643
01:12:28,385 --> 01:12:31,635
Where did you hear about that?

644
01:12:32,845 --> 01:12:35,305
The other detective told me.

645
01:12:39,355 --> 01:12:42,935
Does it bother you,
talking about your wife?

646
01:12:50,406 --> 01:12:54,246
Anyway, there'll be lots of time.

647
01:12:56,076 --> 01:12:58,246
You can't get out of here.

648
01:12:58,746 --> 01:13:02,496
-It's you who wants out.
-I know what you did.

649
01:13:02,586 --> 01:13:06,876
Tell me whatever you like.
That's why you came, isn't it?

650
01:13:10,796 --> 01:13:16,176
You planted hypnotic suggestions
in those people's minds.

651
01:13:16,265 --> 01:13:19,765
It's hard to be a
detective with a crazy wife.

652
01:13:19,855 --> 01:13:20,895
Shut up.

653
01:13:20,975 --> 01:13:25,735
You do it by keeping your work and
your family life completely separate.

654
01:13:25,815 --> 01:13:27,525
How did you do it?

655
01:13:27,605 --> 01:13:32,576
The detective or the
husband, which is the real you?

656
01:13:32,656 --> 01:13:34,826
How did you hypnotize them?

657
01:13:34,906 --> 01:13:37,156
Neither one is the real you.

658
01:13:38,116 --> 01:13:40,326
There is no real you.

659
01:13:41,666 --> 01:13:43,206
Your wife knows that, too.

660
01:13:43,296 --> 01:13:45,206
How did you hypnotize them?

661
01:13:47,086 --> 01:13:48,256
Watch.

662
01:13:52,796 --> 01:13:54,095
You're right.

663
01:13:55,095 --> 01:13:59,635
My wife is a burden. I know.
You don't have to tell me!

664
01:14:01,935 --> 01:14:03,355
I'm a detective.

665
01:14:04,105 --> 01:14:08,565
I've been taught never to show
emotion, even with my family.

666
01:14:08,645 --> 01:14:11,656
And this is the result.

667
01:14:17,036 --> 01:14:19,246
I don't understand her.

668
01:14:19,826 --> 01:14:22,876
She doesn't understand what I go through.

669
01:14:23,456 --> 01:14:27,126
I know it's my fault that it's that way.
So what?

670
01:14:27,206 --> 01:14:28,666
What else could you do?

671
01:14:28,756 --> 01:14:31,836
That's right! What other way is there?

672
01:14:35,555 --> 01:14:36,635
Look,

673
01:14:37,676 --> 01:14:42,055
you think this is how I wanted to end up?

674
01:14:42,555 --> 01:14:47,275
We should all relax, enjoy
ourselves, lead peaceful lives.

675
01:14:47,355 --> 01:14:49,185
But society isn't like that!

676
01:14:50,485 --> 01:14:54,445
Oh, so society's to blame.

677
01:14:55,445 --> 01:14:57,406
It's people like you.

678
01:14:58,496 --> 01:15:05,036
It's guys like you who have
my head about to split open!

679
01:15:07,376 --> 01:15:12,546
Lunatics like you have it easy
while citizens like me go through hell!

680
01:15:13,796 --> 01:15:17,845
I spend my whole life taking
care of that wife of mine!

681
01:15:34,695 --> 01:15:36,275
If it weren't for you...

682
01:15:39,406 --> 01:15:42,406
things would be fine with my wife and me.

683
01:15:47,086 --> 01:15:49,086
Her I can forgive...

684
01:15:51,506 --> 01:15:53,796
but you I can't.

685
01:16:04,225 --> 01:16:05,725
You're amazing.

686
01:16:15,945 --> 01:16:18,065
You like that? Hearing me talk?

687
01:16:19,025 --> 01:16:20,156
Yeah.

688
01:16:23,786 --> 01:16:25,206
Good.

689
01:16:26,666 --> 01:16:28,786
Now it's your turn.
I want the whole story.

690
01:16:30,796 --> 01:16:32,626
All of it.

691
01:16:37,385 --> 01:16:38,506
What's wrong?

692
01:16:42,805 --> 01:16:44,935
Can't talk without your lighter?

693
01:16:50,895 --> 01:16:51,975
Here.

694
01:17:01,156 --> 01:17:02,945
You're amazing.

695
01:17:57,756 --> 01:18:02,926
The water will make you calm.

696
01:18:07,555 --> 01:18:11,805
It will make you happy, empty.

697
01:18:14,565 --> 01:18:19,065
You'll be born again, just like me.

698
01:18:39,336 --> 01:18:40,926
Are you all right?

699
01:18:42,006 --> 01:18:43,086
Was it you?

700
01:18:44,796 --> 01:18:47,055
Did you tell him about me?

701
01:18:47,716 --> 01:18:52,225
Uh, well, you know, he keeps
asking all these questions...

702
01:19:04,656 --> 01:19:08,286
Mesmer was an 18th-century
Austrian doctor,

703
01:19:09,246 --> 01:19:11,536
the first man to study hypnosis.

704
01:19:13,166 --> 01:19:16,626
It wasn't recognized then
as a medical treatment.

705
01:19:17,416 --> 01:19:21,716
They saw it as fakery, magic,

706
01:19:22,216 --> 01:19:23,756
or witchcraft.

707
01:19:25,756 --> 01:19:27,055
And?

708
01:19:27,135 --> 01:19:30,305
There's still a lot we
don't know about Mesmer.

709
01:19:31,135 --> 01:19:34,395
Some say he really did
study magic and alchemy.

710
01:19:37,185 --> 01:19:39,565
And Mamiya's doing that?

711
01:19:40,185 --> 01:19:41,775
Impossible.

712
01:19:42,735 --> 01:19:47,366
If so, the diagnosis would be simple.

713
01:19:48,116 --> 01:19:52,116
He'd simply be a megalomaniac.

714
01:19:53,826 --> 01:19:55,036
But that's not it.

715
01:19:55,956 --> 01:20:00,376
He has definitely lost his memory,
but otherwise he's not abnormal.

716
01:20:01,506 --> 01:20:06,546
But he's also a man with
a very complex personality.

717
01:20:08,506 --> 01:20:11,466
I see. Okay.

718
01:20:18,475 --> 01:20:19,725
Takabe.

719
01:20:21,605 --> 01:20:23,275
Don't talk to him.

720
01:20:24,355 --> 01:20:26,315
You don't know what could happen.

721
01:20:27,985 --> 01:20:29,195
Don't get in too deep.

722
01:20:31,116 --> 01:20:32,286
I know.

723
01:21:07,445 --> 01:21:08,445
Takabe.

724
01:21:15,746 --> 01:21:21,456
Mr. Mamiya, could you tell
us your name or date of birth?

725
01:21:22,456 --> 01:21:24,456
Anything you remember.

726
01:21:30,966 --> 01:21:32,135
Well?

727
01:21:32,676 --> 01:21:36,385
Do you remember anything about yourself?

728
01:21:40,095 --> 01:21:41,145
No.

729
01:21:41,935 --> 01:21:43,145
Mr. Mamiya,

730
01:21:44,145 --> 01:21:48,315
are you aware of the
situation you are in at present?

731
01:21:50,616 --> 01:21:53,195
I mean the charges against you.

732
01:21:55,536 --> 01:21:56,826
Who are you?

733
01:21:57,866 --> 01:21:59,786
Fujiwara, from headquarters.

734
01:22:01,286 --> 01:22:02,706
Well, Mr. Mamiya?

735
01:22:03,916 --> 01:22:08,216
Do you understand why you're here now?

736
01:22:08,716 --> 01:22:10,126
What?

737
01:22:10,216 --> 01:22:12,756
Don't ask questions, answer them.

738
01:22:12,845 --> 01:22:14,135
What questions?

739
01:22:14,635 --> 01:22:15,765
Mr. Mamiya,

740
01:22:16,975 --> 01:22:20,845
incitement to murder can
carry the death penalty.

741
01:22:21,555 --> 01:22:24,065
Do you understand that?

742
01:22:24,145 --> 01:22:25,975
Is that your boss?

743
01:22:26,475 --> 01:22:27,645
Yes.

744
01:22:29,985 --> 01:22:31,485
That must be a drag.

745
01:22:31,565 --> 01:22:34,616
Mr. Mamiya, answer my question.

746
01:22:35,616 --> 01:22:36,945
Who are you?

747
01:22:38,246 --> 01:22:41,076
-Fujiwara. Headquarters.
-Who?

748
01:22:41,166 --> 01:22:43,416
-Are you being smart?
-Who are you?

749
01:22:46,796 --> 01:22:49,836
Takabe, what's wrong with this man?

750
01:22:50,336 --> 01:22:52,966
-I'm asking who you are.
-Answer my question!

751
01:22:53,926 --> 01:22:57,466
All right, I'll ask you again.

752
01:22:59,345 --> 01:23:01,305
Fujiwara-of-Headquarters.

753
01:23:02,805 --> 01:23:04,105
Who are you?

754
01:23:06,815 --> 01:23:10,525
What... exactly do you mean?

755
01:23:12,565 --> 01:23:14,565
You think about that.

756
01:23:20,996 --> 01:23:22,246
I'm very sorry!

757
01:23:23,206 --> 01:23:26,416
You must understand, he has amnesia.

758
01:23:29,546 --> 01:23:31,376
What a bunch.

759
01:23:35,546 --> 01:23:37,756
They don't understand, do they?

760
01:23:39,885 --> 01:23:41,265
About me,

761
01:23:42,265 --> 01:23:43,645
or about you.

762
01:23:48,355 --> 01:23:52,855
Detective, do you hear my voice?

763
01:23:55,985 --> 01:23:57,366
You do, don't you?

764
01:24:00,076 --> 01:24:04,456
That proves you're a special person.

765
01:24:08,246 --> 01:24:10,126
You knew that from the start.

766
01:24:12,666 --> 01:24:14,336
So did I.

767
01:24:16,546 --> 01:24:18,635
You're different from them.

768
01:24:22,926 --> 01:24:24,265
You're someone

769
01:24:25,515 --> 01:24:30,105
who can understand what I'm really saying.

770
01:24:37,025 --> 01:24:38,025
Take him away.

771
01:26:55,336 --> 01:26:57,256
Will Okinawa be warm?

772
01:27:00,876 --> 01:27:02,635
Let's eat lots of good food.

773
01:27:05,426 --> 01:27:07,765
What do you want to eat?

774
01:27:10,595 --> 01:27:14,145
Fumie, we're not going to Okinawa.

775
01:27:15,725 --> 01:27:16,815
I know.

776
01:27:25,775 --> 01:27:30,406
The sea there must be beautiful.

777
01:27:36,376 --> 01:27:39,046
Just until my work settles down.

778
01:27:40,336 --> 01:27:41,756
I understand.

779
01:27:42,336 --> 01:27:43,626
I'll take her bag.

780
01:27:44,716 --> 01:27:46,216
Shall we go?

781
01:27:51,475 --> 01:27:53,975
Thank you, Doctor.

782
01:27:56,765 --> 01:27:58,225
Mr. Takabe.

783
01:28:00,315 --> 01:28:02,815
It's not good to work too hard.

784
01:28:05,315 --> 01:28:09,695
You look sicker than your wife to me.

785
01:28:16,286 --> 01:28:20,586
I'm sorry, I don't have the tag.
I wonder where it went.

786
01:28:21,086 --> 01:28:24,426
-A week ago, wasn't it?
-Yes.

787
01:28:25,966 --> 01:28:27,506
Mr. Takabe?

788
01:28:27,595 --> 01:28:29,756
One moment, please.

789
01:28:48,235 --> 01:28:50,445
I'm sorry, sir, but it's not here.

790
01:28:51,485 --> 01:28:53,326
That can't be.

791
01:28:55,156 --> 01:28:57,786
Maybe you took it somewhere else?

792
01:28:57,876 --> 01:28:58,996
No.

793
01:28:59,086 --> 01:29:01,206
Or you gave it to your wife.

794
01:29:01,296 --> 01:29:02,546
No.

795
01:29:12,555 --> 01:29:14,135
May I take your plate?

796
01:29:15,975 --> 01:29:17,185
Yes.

797
01:29:27,195 --> 01:29:28,355
Yeah?

798
01:29:29,695 --> 01:29:30,906
Sakuma?

799
01:29:32,576 --> 01:29:33,735
What?

800
01:29:35,656 --> 01:29:37,246
No, I'm not busy.

801
01:29:39,206 --> 01:29:40,206
Now?

802
01:29:46,836 --> 01:29:48,966
I want to show you something.

803
01:29:49,635 --> 01:29:50,796
What?

804
01:29:50,885 --> 01:29:55,176
A film on hypnotherapy.
The university put it on video.

805
01:29:58,225 --> 01:30:03,815
The oldest material on hypnotism in Japan.

806
01:30:05,775 --> 01:30:10,105
It probably dates from
the end of the 19th century.

807
01:30:21,416 --> 01:30:23,706
Watch the man's hand.

808
01:30:27,256 --> 01:30:31,176
You have to look closely. See? There.

809
01:30:31,966 --> 01:30:34,805
You see what looks like an X?

810
01:30:49,065 --> 01:30:51,315
-That's it?
-Yeah.

811
01:30:52,406 --> 01:30:53,656
What does it mean?

812
01:30:54,576 --> 01:30:59,406
Her name was Suzu Murakawa.
She was treated for hysteria.

813
01:30:59,996 --> 01:31:01,956
That's all that's recorded.

814
01:31:04,286 --> 01:31:06,666
Police records say...

815
01:31:08,796 --> 01:31:15,046
she was arrested for the
murder of her son in 1898.

816
01:31:17,926 --> 01:31:21,725
She seems to have killed him

817
01:31:22,265 --> 01:31:26,895
by carving the shape
of a cross into his neck.

818
01:31:29,185 --> 01:31:31,105
That's all we know.

819
01:31:32,695 --> 01:31:35,116
Did Mamiya see this film?

820
01:31:35,866 --> 01:31:37,195
I don't know.

821
01:31:37,945 --> 01:31:41,746
There's not much chance even
medical students would see it.

822
01:31:43,036 --> 01:31:46,876
But even if he had,

823
01:31:48,206 --> 01:31:52,876
that still wouldn't explain his actions.

824
01:31:57,676 --> 01:32:00,176
Who's this man in the film?

825
01:32:01,515 --> 01:32:02,685
Unknown.

826
01:32:03,725 --> 01:32:09,185
We do know, however, why he
didn't show his face to the camera.

827
01:32:11,935 --> 01:32:17,025
You know what they called
hypnotism in Japan back then?

828
01:32:19,985 --> 01:32:21,326
"Soul conjuring."

829
01:32:22,406 --> 01:32:26,376
Like clairvoyance,
spiritualism — that sort of thing.

830
01:32:28,456 --> 01:32:34,086
The authorities in any age
always suppress occultism...

831
01:32:36,426 --> 01:32:41,265
and the Meiji government back then
would have suppressed this technique.

832
01:32:42,426 --> 01:32:48,265
It would only have been
performed in secret ceremonies.

833
01:33:34,275 --> 01:33:37,315
HERESIES

834
01:33:43,036 --> 01:33:47,156
CHAPTER 4 — MESMER

835
01:33:49,626 --> 01:33:53,166
TOJIRO HAKURAKU DOB UNKNOWN,
DIED IN 1898

836
01:35:39,275 --> 01:35:40,435
Sakuma.

837
01:35:50,656 --> 01:35:51,656
Huh?

838
01:35:52,616 --> 01:35:55,876
So what is Mamiya, then?

839
01:35:57,836 --> 01:36:00,706
What's your guess? Tell me.

840
01:36:02,836 --> 01:36:04,176
A missionary.

841
01:36:05,466 --> 01:36:06,796
A missionary?

842
01:36:08,256 --> 01:36:11,635
Sent to propagate the ceremony.

843
01:36:16,935 --> 01:36:20,225
Sorry, I was just imagining things.

844
01:36:22,485 --> 01:36:24,695
What am I saying?

845
01:36:25,315 --> 01:36:28,326
Don't take me seriously.

846
01:36:29,906 --> 01:36:31,536
I'm a little tired.

847
01:36:33,156 --> 01:36:35,206
Let's call it a day.

848
01:36:35,956 --> 01:36:38,996
Now I'm getting in too deep.

849
01:36:48,796 --> 01:36:52,015
Sakuma, what's that?

850
01:37:00,565 --> 01:37:03,105
Oh, that?

851
01:37:03,985 --> 01:37:07,406
I just thought it might help me to think.

852
01:37:07,906 --> 01:37:09,235
About what?

853
01:37:10,445 --> 01:37:13,116
About...

854
01:37:15,826 --> 01:37:17,116
I don't know.

855
01:37:23,756 --> 01:37:25,796
You met Mamiya, didn't you?

856
01:37:25,876 --> 01:37:27,126
No.

857
01:37:29,006 --> 01:37:30,095
Yes, you did.

858
01:37:32,055 --> 01:37:33,385
It's weird.

859
01:37:35,635 --> 01:37:37,095
I don't remember.

860
01:39:39,176 --> 01:39:42,225
Kunihiko Mamiya's whereabouts unknown.

861
01:39:42,305 --> 01:39:48,685
Earlier reports of him near
Kawasaki Station were inaccurate.

862
01:39:49,185 --> 01:39:52,195
In the absence of further information,

863
01:39:52,275 --> 01:39:56,826
the search area is being
widened from Tokyo and Saitama

864
01:39:56,906 --> 01:39:59,695
to the entire Kanto plain.

865
01:40:01,036 --> 01:40:02,156
Hello?

866
01:40:03,116 --> 01:40:05,036
One moment, please.

867
01:40:05,916 --> 01:40:07,916
Mr. Takabe, it's for you.

868
01:40:09,416 --> 01:40:10,586
Hello?

869
01:40:12,586 --> 01:40:14,086
I see.

870
01:40:15,756 --> 01:40:17,885
We're on our way.

871
01:40:43,956 --> 01:40:47,246
Dr. Sakuma's body has
been taken to the hospital.

872
01:40:48,666 --> 01:40:53,046
It was probably suicide.
He strangled himself.

873
01:40:55,216 --> 01:40:57,385
He'd cuffed himself to that pipe,

874
01:40:58,296 --> 01:40:59,805
strange as that sounds.

875
01:44:01,525 --> 01:44:03,815
So you've come, Detective.

876
01:44:16,786 --> 01:44:18,666
Why did you let me escape?

877
01:44:23,796 --> 01:44:25,216
You know why?

878
01:44:26,966 --> 01:44:32,595
By letting me escape, you
could learn my true secret.

879
01:44:34,225 --> 01:44:35,805
All by yourself.

880
01:44:40,645 --> 01:44:42,895
You didn't have to, though.

881
01:44:45,315 --> 01:44:51,286
Anyone who wants to meet his
true self is bound to come here.

882
01:44:52,326 --> 01:44:54,036
It's fate.

883
01:45:14,515 --> 01:45:15,765
Remember now?

884
01:45:17,765 --> 01:45:20,605
Do you remember everything?

885
01:45:28,735 --> 01:45:29,906
You do?

886
01:45:32,326 --> 01:45:35,786
This is the end for you, too.

887
01:46:48,445 --> 01:46:51,195
Fearsome... heart of...

888
01:46:51,866 --> 01:46:53,945
His... healing hand.

889
01:46:54,025 --> 01:46:57,286
Road of healing... Not a long...

890
01:46:57,366 --> 01:46:59,996
Take sword...

891
01:47:00,496 --> 01:47:03,836
A man... but dew.

892
01:47:03,916 --> 01:47:09,216
Heal, O... water grass! O winter...

893
01:47:09,296 --> 01:47:10,796
falls... snow.

894
01:47:10,876 --> 01:47:12,385
That... heal... snow.

895
01:47:12,466 --> 01:47:14,845
Take... in hand... heal.

896
01:47:47,496 --> 01:47:49,006
Shall I bring your coffee?

897
01:47:54,385 --> 01:47:55,506
Yes?

898
01:47:58,385 --> 01:48:02,055
All right. Bring the car around.

899
01:48:21,956 --> 01:48:23,286
Here you are.

900
01:48:24,036 --> 01:48:25,786
-Thanks.
-You're welcome.

901
01:49:33,435 --> 01:49:36,195
KOJI YAKUSHO

